= Solution
{parent=b}

**This sequence does occur**, for the oriented <connected sum>
$$
\boxed{M=(S^1\times S^3)\#(S^1\times S^3).}
$$
The <Kunneth theorem> gives one copy of $\mathbb Z$ in dimensions $0,1,3,4$ for each factor product and zero in dimension two. Removing a disc from each summand and gluing their boundary three-spheres, the <Mayer-Vietoris sequence> makes the <homology> in dimensions one through three the direct sum of that of the two summands. The two <orientations> join to one top <fundamental class>, so $H_0=H_4=\mathbb Z$, $H_1=H_3=\mathbb Z^2$, and $H_2=0$.

